> how can i solve this error There are too many executions running simultaneously for this Apps Script project at
  this time in autocart excel

● This error occurs when your Google Apps Script project hits the concurrent execution limit. Google Apps Script has
  quotas that restrict how many instances of a script can run at the same time.

  Causes

  - Multiple users triggering the script simultaneously
  - Triggers firing too frequently (time-driven or spreadsheet triggers)
  - Long-running scripts that overlap with new executions
  - Loops or recursive calls spawning multiple executions

  Solutions

  1. Add Lock Service to prevent concurrent runs

  function myFunction() {
    var lock = LockService.getScriptLock();
    try {
      // Wait up to 30 seconds for the lock
      lock.waitLock(30000);

      // Your code here

    } catch (e) {
      Logger.log('Could not obtain lock: ' + e);
    } finally {
      lock.releaseLock();
    }
  }

  2. Reduce trigger frequency

  - If using time-driven triggers, increase the interval between runs
  - Check Edit > Current project's triggers and remove duplicate triggers

  3. Optimize script performance

  - Batch read/write operations instead of cell-by-cell
  - Use getValues() and setValues() for ranges instead of loops
  - Minimize API calls

  4. Add delays between operations

  Utilities.sleep(1000); // Wait 1 second between operations

  5. Check for runaway triggers

  Go to Executions in the Apps Script editor to see if scripts are stacking up, and cancel unnecessary ones.

